/T (Compensate for the weaknesses of the model by feeding it the outputs of other tools. For example, a text retrieval system \(sometimes called RAG or retrieval augmented generation\) can tell the model about relevant documents. A code execution engine like OpenAl's Code Interpreter can help the model do math and run code. If a task can be done more reliably or efficiently by a tool rather than by a language model, offload it to get the best of both.)
/E (Compensate for the weaknesses of the model by feeding it the outputs of other tools. For example, a text retrieval system \(sometimes called RAG or retrieval augmented generation\) can tell the model about relevant documents. A code execution engine like OpenAl's Code Interpreter can help the model do math and run code. If a task can be done more reliably or efficiently by a tool rather than by a language model, offload it to get the best of both.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [23]
>>
